# Club acceptance test - scenes, sequences and positioning

Run this checklist once in order. Later tests reuse earlier scenes rather than
repeating setup. Record PASS/FAIL beside each section and describe any difference.
Do not delete or overwrite your existing show scenes or room definitions.

## 0. Prepare safely

1. Allow enough time with no audience. Tell anyone present that heads may move.
2. Verify LichtWerk's configured output is universe 5 only. Lighting fixtures occupy
   addresses 1-98; haze pump/fan are addresses 99/100. Resolume's universes are not
   part of this test.
3. Before starting the backend, check the physical heads' paths are clear. On startup,
   BLACKOUT must be active, heads must use their saved rest, pump/fan must be zero,
   and no sequence may start.
4. Open the Controller page and connect APC40 MKII. Leave the browser open for all
   hardware-created dialogs. Confirm the page identifies REAL OUTPUT only when the
   configured adapter is healthy. Do not retry output if its universe is uncertain.
5. Keep blackout active for authoring and permission tests. Haze is independent of
   blackout/master: leave haze zero and skip the optional haze section if unsuitable.
6. Confirm room calibration is valid and all temporary safety overrides are OFF.
   Never enable an override to make a failed test pass.

## 1. Position permissions versus aim (APC40 and screen)

Use the moving-head group. Write down its current included/excluded zones so they
can be restored at the end. Use two known, reachable zones, here called X and Y.

1. Hold SHIFT and press the group's TRACK SELECT (track 2); release SHIFT.
   The positioning menu must open in AIM mode.
2. Press DOWN (or PERMISSIONS on screen). Without starting Move FX, note both heads'
   current position and press X repeatedly. It must cycle:
   not included -> included -> explicitly excluded -> not included.
   Skip forward to not included first if X began in another state.
   No press may move either head. Screen text/markers must match the hardware:
   dim neutral = not included; cyan = included; red = explicitly excluded.
3. Include X and Y, one press each from not included. Both must remain included.
4. Press UP (AIM). Press X, then Y. Each deliberate aim moves the heads to that
   zone's centre; permissions must remain X and Y, not only the most recent zone.
5. Return to PERMISSIONS and explicitly exclude X. Return to AIM and aim at X.
   The heads may travel there, but the beam must remain dark while excluded.
   Re-include X in PERMISSIONS: the heads must not jump to its centre.
6. Close and reopen the menu using SHIFT + TRACK SELECT. It must default to AIM,
   regardless of the previous mode.
7. SHIFT + an existing target pad, then an existing zone pad: each must open that
   exact entry for editing, not recall it or alter permissions. Cancel both.
   Press an empty target pad, then an empty zone pad: the correct Add dialog opens.
   Cancel; no definitions or assignments should have changed.
8. With X and Y included, open Move from SCENE LAUNCH 3 and launch its first Circle preset.
   Both included zone pads must be fully lit; the tour must visit both.
   Stop it using TRACK SELECT to choose the strip and STOP ALL CLIPS.
   This button must still stop FX, not a scene sequence.

## 2. Create reusable selective scenes

Use names prefixed TEST so cleanup is unambiguous. Choose unused scene pads.

1. Select the DJ-spots group and set a low intensity and red colour. Press an empty
   scene pad: the scene editor must open. Save TEST Spots Red containing ONLY the
   DJ spots and their intensity/main colour. Exclude heads, LED bar and haze.
2. Prepare TEST Heads X: heads group, low intensity/main colour and named zone X,
   with X and Y included and no extra exclusions. Save on another empty pad.
3. Prepare TEST Heads Y: the same group/attributes, but zone Y and another colour.
   Explicitly select Seconds and set an incoming fade of 2 seconds (new scenes
   default to beats). Save on a third pad.
4. Prepare TEST Split: head 1 -> X and head 2 -> Y as individual positioning entries.
   Do not substitute the group entry. Save on another pad.
5. SHIFT + TEST Heads Y: its saved values must appear without recalling the scene.
   Change its name, save, and verify it remains on the same pad with the same ID.
6. If capturing from preview, confirm the editor explicitly identifies Preview as
   the source. Captured values must exclude master/blackout/FLASH/FX modulation.
7. Return to live. Release blackout only after checking directions and low levels.
   Recall TEST Heads X then TEST Spots Red: heads must keep their state.
   Recall TEST Split: head 1 aims at X and head 2 at Y.
8. Press TEST Split again: it must recall again, never switch other lights off.
   Fixture badges/details must identify the affected fixtures unambiguously.
9. Change the positioning menu's prior zone selections, then recall TEST Heads X.
   Its saved permissions must replace the prior selection and feedback must agree.
   No transition may illuminate forbidden travel or exceed mechanical limits.

## 3. Manual adjustment and authoring clarity

1. Recall TEST Heads X. Try manually changing a head's scene-controlled colour.
   Use APC40 group COLOR pads/saturation and its intensity fader; repeat one change
   on screen. Both must work immediately without Release. Saved scene values must
   remain unchanged. Recall again to restore the saved look deliberately.
2. On screen, edit TEST Split using controller-order columns. Set colour at head
   GROUP level and intensity separately for head 1 and head 2. The same parameter
   must not simultaneously be set at group and individual levels without an
   explicit resolution. Verify different individual intensities survive Save/recall.
3. Enter intensity 101% or an invalid name/number. The field must explain the problem
   immediately and Save must not accept it. Correct to 25%: the recalled level and
   on-screen fader must agree. Units must be visible, not unexplained 0-1 values.
4. Choose a zone aim in the scene editor: that zone must automatically be permitted.
   Other permissions should stay collapsed under Include other zones. Expand only
   when testing additional Move FX areas; no zone-spot u/v fields should be shown.
5. For an existing saved non-centre zone spot, open/save without changing its zone:
   its existing position must survive, even though its spot fields are hidden.
6. Recall a scene; edit one saved value without Apply now. Output must not change.
   Use Apply now explicitly: the edited scene must then be recalled.
7. Briefly test master, blackout and FLASH. They must retain their normal priority
   and must not rewrite the saved scene. Stop any FX before continuing.

## 4. Seconds sequence and independent static scene

1. Open SEQUENCES using RIGHT. Create TEST Tour from an empty pad.
   Add TEST Heads X then TEST Heads Y. Set timing mode Seconds, Loop, fade inherited,
   and 3 seconds hold AFTER each fade.
2. Duplicate a step, reorder with up/down, then remove the duplicate. Confirm the
   resulting order is X, Y and the source scenes' fades were not changed.
3. Start TEST Tour. A step with a 2-second fade and 3-second hold must occupy about
   5 seconds, not 3. Observe at least two complete loops, including Y -> X.
   While it runs, manually change a controlled intensity. The change must work;
   the next step may write its saved intensity again.
4. Press its running pad: pause. Heads and step/fade/hold progress must freeze.
   Press again: resume from that phase, not step 1.
5. While a fade is running, press RECORD (sequence Stop). Values must freeze,
   without blackout or rolling back. Start again, then SHIFT + PLAY: restart at X.
6. Recall TEST Spots Red while TEST Tour runs. The sequence must continue, since
   DJ spots do not overlap its controlled attributes.
7. Recall TEST Heads X manually. The overlapping sequence must stop before recall.
8. Start TEST Tour again, switch to colour/FX/position pages: playback status must
   remain visible. Left/right navigation changes pages only, not playback.
9. Edit TEST Heads Y while TEST Tour runs. The current run must keep its snapshot;
   a restart/new launch must use the changed definition. Apply now is deliberate.
10. Change TEST Tour to One-shot and start. After its final fade/hold it must finish,
    retaining final values and never looping or blacking out automatically.
11. In the sequence editor, set Live controls -> Moving heads -> Main colour.
    Before starting, pick blue on the APC40 heads-group COLOR page. Start TEST Tour:
    it must keep blue through both X/Y positions despite their saved colours.
    Pick red during playback: both heads must keep red across subsequent steps.
    Stop using RECORD, then recall TEST Heads Y directly: its own saved colour
    must apply, proving the sequence's Live setting did not leak into direct scenes.
12. After Stop, move the group intensity/colour controls immediately. No Release
    action must be needed. Unrelated static-scene fades must not be cancelled by Stop.

## 5. Beat sequence and Speed label

1. Create a temporary scene: its fade unit must initially be Beats, with Cut and
   1/2, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 choices. A new sequence must default to Beats too.
   Set a standalone 4-beat fade; change BPM halfway through: it must preserve
   progress and finish at the new speed. Existing 2-second scenes must remain seconds.
   Then edit TEST Tour to Beats. Choose the supported beat durations; verify choices are
   1/2, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32. Set a short hold and an inherited nonzero scene fade.
2. At 120 BPM, a 2-second inherited fade must convert upward to 4 beats.
   A zero fade must stay a cut. Inherited durations above 32 beats must clamp to 32.
3. Start in Loop mode. Change BPM during a fade and during a hold: progress must
   continue smoothly in beats at the new speed, without restarting the current step.
4. Pause, change BPM, resume: no missed-step burst or phase reset.
5. Open Move (SCENE LAUNCH 3) and select its strip. The knob must show Rate at the
   normal label size and beats/cycle as the smaller text below, without overflow.
   Changing BPM still affects both beat sequences and FX.

## 5a. Family FX presets and creative controls

Use LED bar track 1 for dimmer/colour tests first. Keep haze zero. For heads use
track 2 (group), measured/calibrated heads and the included test areas from section 1.
These checks use universe 5: bar 1-6, heads 7-80, spots 81-98; no haze commands.
Do not treat lighting blackout as preventing head movement.

1. On APC40 press SCENE LAUNCH 1, 2, 3: screen must show Dimmer, Colour, Move.
   Buttons 4/5 must do nothing and remain dark. Each family has five rows of
   presets aligned with their track columns; standby/incompatible fixture columns
   remain dark. Only family buttons belong in the SCENE LAUNCH column: its unused
   fourth/fifth cells must never contain FX presets. Select individual heads/spots
   with their numbered buttons: exactly five presets must appear in each active
   compatible individual column and disappear from the corresponding group column.
   Switch back to groups and verify the reverse. Start/stop one pad
   twice and verify its running indication changes. TRACK SELECT 1 selects bar
   knobs; STOP ALL CLIPS stops only that strip's FX, not a running scene sequence.
2. Press SCENE LAUNCH 1, TRACK SELECT 1, then screen Edit FX presets. Select slot 1,
   name it TEST Triangle, Shape Triangle, base-relative minimum 20%, maximum 100%,
   cycle 4 beats, Spread 0. Save: this must not launch. Launch from row 1/column 1.
   At bar fader 80%, output must remain between 16% and 80% before master. Change
   fader to 50%: range becomes 10%-50%. Zero fader stays dark. FLASH may override
   dimming while held; release restores modulation, not a saved old intensity.
3. Use knob 2 (Depth), then Store current FX for slot 1. Its displayed minimum
   must follow depth. Change Shape to Saw up and Save while running: Triangle must
   continue. Save & Apply now must deliberately switch. Stop FX: latest bar fader
   value returns immediately. Verify the source scene stayed unchanged.
4. Enter an out-of-range percentage/invalid duration: immediate error and Save
   disabled. Switch a dimmer to a quarter-beat cycle and a sufficiently high BPM:
   when fewer than four output frames fit a cycle, a timing warning must appear.
   Do not use this as a software strobe test; restore 120 BPM and a slow rate.
5. Select heads group track 2, Dimmer. In More, inspect fixture order by names.
   Use All + Spread 100%: two heads pulse half a cycle apart. Spread 0 synchronizes.
   Reverse the order and compare. Odd/Even selects only one head; the other keeps
   its base output. Alternating uses both with opposing phases. One by one is
   distinct from a generic square wave. Restore All. Single-fixture Spread must
   be unavailable/explained, not pretend to create a multi-head wave.
6. Change the bar's saved dimmer timing to Seconds, 4 seconds/cycle. Launch, then
   change BPM from 120 to 90: this FX must keep its four-second cycle. Change
   seconds rate during the run: progress must not reset to the start.
7. SCENE LAUNCH 2, bar track 1. Select Follow base Two colours via factory chooser,
   launch and use COLOR to change base colour: the look must follow. Open editor
   and choose Fixed palette [blue, magenta, red], Smooth, 8 beats/cycle. Apply now:
   palette must traverse all colours including last-to-first. Switch to Step and
   compare. Base colour changes must not filter/remove palette colours; intensity
   still works. Screen explains the fixed palette's ownership. Repeat briefly
   on a Q-Spot: main white is zero while palette runs and returns to current base
   white after Stop. Ring channels must not be changed by this colour effect.
8. While dimmer runs, start Colour and Move on a head: all three families coexist.
   Launch another Colour slot: only the old Colour is replaced. Do the same for
   Move: no hidden Circle + Figure 8 combination remains from an earlier slot.
   Pad LEDs and running status must agree. Switch group/single and back: remembered
   group/single effects must suspend/reactivate correctly without double owners.
9. In Move choose an existing Circle factory, set alternate-head X reflection and
   Spread 0. Compare with Normal and with the old Mirror factory (phase offset):
   reflection and phase offset must not be described as identical. Beam permissions
   remain active; never enlarge areas just to make an invalid pattern appear lit.
10. Save the TEST slots, stop FX, ensure haze zero/blackout, then restart backend
    once alongside the other restart checks in section 7. Presets must survive
    and no FX must start automatically. Fixture renaming must not lose slots.
    Reset a TEST slot to factory and verify the saved override is removed without
    silently changing a running snapshot.

## 5b. Target Tour and combined movement

1. Keep measured targets X/Y available (substitute two existing measured target
   names, not the similarly named areas). On APC40 SCENE LAUNCH 3, TRACK SELECT 2,
   open Edit FX presets, slot 5. Name it TEST Target Tour. Select Target Tour,
   add targets X then Y, travel 4 beats, hold 4 beats, Pattern None. Save & Apply
   now. Heads must travel to X, hold precisely, travel to Y, hold, and repeat.
   Travel uses normal beam protection: an allowed endpoint never illuminates
   an undefined/excluded route. FLASH must not bypass mandatory dark protection.
   Device knob 1 must read Travel with beats/travel. Turn it: travel duration
   changes, not Hold or the optional pattern Rate. Repeat with seconds timing:
   seconds/travel must appear and changing it must not restart the tour.
2. With the destination target inside permitted areas, change Pattern to Circle,
   small Size, Apply now. Heads must travel without circles, circle during the
   hold, then travel without circles again. Test Figure 8 similarly. A target
   outside permitted areas must reject a patterned tour with an actionable error;
   the previous valid run must remain. Pattern None may use a reachable stationary
   target outside included areas, but only the exact hold endpoint may be lit.
3. During this Move tour start an existing colour/intensity scene sequence. The
   tour continues independently. Run Dimmer and Colour families too if desired.
   Stop the sequence: tour continues. Stop Move: current underlying base aim
   returns, without resetting colour/intensity or stored scene definitions.
4. Reorder X/Y in the editor and Save: current tour remains its launch snapshot.
   Apply now restarts deliberately with the new order. While the tour runs, try
   changing its target coordinates or room size: actionable Stop-first error.
   Saved tour references prevent target deletion even after Stop until removed
   from the preset. An uncalibrated/unreachable target or empty selection must
   not partially launch a group or stop the prior valid effect.
5. Repeat a seconds-based tour through Preview/Go in section 6. Confirm both the
   current target/travel/hold phase and pattern phase survive Go, without step 1
   restarting and without any earlier live output change. Tempo stays live.

## 5c. Fusion Orbit rings: manual controls, segment FX and scenes

These are real-output tests only when deliberately enabled at the club. The
current 37ch patch uses universe 5: head 1 starts at 7, head 2 at 44. Ring
intensity is DMX 19/56, ring strobe 20/57, section RGB ranges 24-41/61-78.
Native ring colour/program/speed channels 21-23/58-60 remain fixed at zero.
Do not change the fixture modes or touch other universes/Resolume.

1. Keep beam faders at zero. Select heads group with numbered button 2.
   Press its physical A/B (screen RING): it lights; nothing emits merely because
   it was selected. COLOR opens ALL and section 1-6 selectors, followed by a
   compact palette. Select ALL, Red, then set the top knob to about 30% ring
   intensity. Both rings should become uniformly red; beams stay off. Confirm
   no fixture-native macro animation overrides the selected RGB.
2. Select section 1 then Blue. Only section 1 on each head changes. Repeat
   sections 2-6 to identify their physical positions; record the actual numbering
   rather than assuming clockwise order. ALL then Green makes every section
   green. Colour selection must not change ring intensity.
3. Return to beam context, set top saturation to 30%, select RING and set its
   intensity to 70%. Toggle back: top indication returns to 30% saturation and
   the ring stays at 70%. Toggle again: indication returns to 70% ring intensity.
   Repeated switching must not change either colour/intensity. Track fader still
   changes beam intensity only. FLASH remains beam-only.
4. With RING active toggle STROBE: only rings strobe. Return to beam context:
   its strobe indication/state remains separate. CUE rate adjusts whichever
   beam/ring strobes are already on without switching others on. Turn both off.
   The Fusion strobe Hz indication remains approximate pending measurement.
5. SCENE LAUNCH 1 selects Dimmer. With track 2 RING active, open Edit FX presets:
   title says Ring, five slots appear, and fixture ordering lists twelve sections.
   Prepare a One by one look with full Spread and visible ring intensity; Apply.
   Confirm sequential segment modulation, including across both heads. Try
   reversing/reordering and Odd/Even. Switch to Colour (SCENE LAUNCH 2), try
   Rainbow with Spread, then an ordered fixed palette. Beam colours/intensity
   must remain unchanged, and ring Dimmer/Colour combine without rewriting base.
6. Turn RING off, run a beam Dimmer/Colour look while ring FX continue. Turn RING
   on and STOP FX: only ring FX stop, restoring current ring base colours.
   Beam FX remain. Turn RING off and STOP FX: existing beam-context stop works.
   Move remains a fixture-level effect, not another six movement participants.
7. With known ring colours/intensity, use an existing permitted movement tour
   through a dark transfer or aim the beam into a forbidden area. Beam protection
   must remain enforced, including under FLASH, while rings stay illuminated.
   Master must scale both beam and ring; BLACKOUT must extinguish both without
   destroying their stored/runtime base values. Restore master/blackout.
8. Use numbered head 1 button 3 to switch to individuals. Group column goes
   standby and individual columns become active. Each compatible active strip
   still has five FX rows. Set different ring looks per head. Return to group
   button 2: remembered group controls/runs resume; switching RING alone never
   recalls any values. Repeat a group/single switch with both component FX running.
9. In Show create/edit a TEST scene, select the head/group ring family. First
   choose Uniform ring or Individual sections; do not show eighteen RGB fields
   immediately. Save a uniform look, then a different TEST six-section look.
   Reopen each without recall: saved values stay unchanged. Merely switching the
   editor view must not flatten a multicolour look. Explicit uniform colour edits
   replace all sections. Capture and a scene sequence must reproduce the sections.
   Sequence Live controls must respect uniform or selected individual ring fields.
10. Enter PREVIEW. Change ring colours/intensity/strobe and start different ring
    FX: live rings must remain unchanged. Check both room monitors: each head
    has six ring sections around its beam dot, showing its respective Live or
    Preview colours/intensity/FX. A dark beam must not hide an illuminated ring.
    Inactive Preview retains dark ring outlines. Ring strobe animates only the
    ring; high rates use the existing screen blink cap. Section order on screen
    is schematic; do not infer physical clockwise orientation from it.
    Master dims both ring drawings; BLACKOUT darkens Live but not active Preview.
    GO promotes staged values/current FX
    phase. Beam and ring FX remain independent. Save a ring preset, restart:
    it survives independently of beam presets, but no FX/ring output auto-starts.
    No persistent haze disclaimer or large FX help paragraph should push the
    device knobs out of view; safety/status labels remain visible.

## 6. Animated preview and exact-phase Go

1. Start TEST Tour live. Enter PREVIEW. Confirm two clearly labelled views:
   Live on the left, Preview on the right.
   Before entering Preview, its room and neutral fixture markers must be visible,
   without live colours, beams, strobe or haze. Both monitors belong in the APC40
   right pane; pads/tracks retain full height and right-pane controls remain scrollable.
   Both monitor headers and room drawings must align horizontally. At the club's
   normal maximized viewport, device knobs must be visible without being pushed
   below an oversized sequence status panel.
2. Prepare a different sequence/step order in Preview. Run it long enough to see
   several animated steps. The physical heads and Live view must continue the
   original live show, unaffected by preview commands or global-mask changes.
3. Pause/resume the preview sequence. Only its timeline should pause/resume.
4. During a nonzero preview fade, press GO. Live must adopt the CURRENT preview
   position/colour/step/fade progress and continue from there, not restart at X.
5. Repeat Go during a hold. Remaining hold time must carry over, not restart.
6. Preview a static scene, hold FLASH, then release: FLASH acts live only while held;
   the staged scene must not be sent before Go. Master/blackout also remain live.

## 7. Definitions, reconnect and restart

1. Try deleting a scene used by TEST Tour. It must be blocked with a useful reference
   message. Try deleting a target/zone referenced by a saved scene: also blocked.
   Cancel; never delete existing production definitions for this test.
   While TEST Tour is running/paused, try editing a referenced destination's geometry:
   it must require Stop first. Display-name edits and runtime safety permissions must
   remain available. Stop before making actual coordinate changes.
2. Unassign one TEST scene pad without deleting its scene. The scene and sequence
   reference must remain available. Reassign that existing scene to an empty pad.
3. While a sequence runs, reload the browser and reconnect APC40. Playback must not
   restart/stop; current page/status/LED feedback must recover.
4. With output blacked out and haze zero, restart the backend manually.
   Definitions and assignments persist, but no sequence starts automatically.
   Heads start at rest; included zones may be restored, but an unreached saved aim
   must not falsely show as reached.
5. Deliberately start Move FX using those restored permissions. A rest position
   outside the included areas alone must not block launch.
6. Only if safe and practical, interrupt configured OLA delivery while running a
   sequence. The error must be visible and playback must pause. Restore OLA/Retry;
   playback requires deliberate resume, not automatic catch-up. Do not disconnect
   or reconfigure Resolume's universes to perform this test.

## 8. Optional haze automation - do not use blackout as a haze stop

Skip if haze operation is not appropriate or the fixture is not ready.

1. Stop other playback. Verify pump/fan are zero. Explicitly opt haze into a TEST
   scene at a low, manufacturer-appropriate setting, then make a second TEST scene
   with pump/fan zero. Do not guess safe warm-up/cooldown timings.
2. Recall each once: only explicitly saved pump/fan values change.
   In Live, small gray bubbles must start at the hazer, grow as they travel and
   fade away at the end. Pump controls brightness, highest at 100%; fan controls
   travel speed, with zero pausing travel. Reduced-motion settings pause travel.
   Enter Preview and change only preview pump/fan: its bubbles must change while
   live output/bubbles stay unchanged. This is a command indicator, not measured fog.
3. If testing haze inside a sequence, include the zero-pump scene and keep Stop
   and the pump fader within reach. Stop freezes current values; it does NOT
   automatically turn haze off. End by explicitly setting pump/fan to zero.
4. Lighting blackout/master must not alter haze; normal HAZE hold must release to
   the underlying value. Follow the hazer's shutdown/cooldown instructions.

## Finish

1. Stop sequences and FX, release holds, explicitly set haze pump/fan zero, and
   enable blackout. Manual controls must remain usable without Release.
2. Restore the original zone permissions recorded at the beginning.
3. Remove TEST sequence references first, then TEST scenes/pad assignments only.
   Keep all original configuration, calibration and production scenes.
4. Record failed section/step, active scene/sequence, live versus preview, controller
   used, displayed error and what the physical fixture did. Do not hide failures by
   changing calibration or disabling protection.
